  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing (NAICS 325412) contracted much less federal work in FY2027 to date than in prior years. The federal government obligated $84.2M in FY2027 to date through 373 awards, with an average award size of $226K. Obligations fell down 99.4% year over year. The fiscal-year series shows much larger totals earlier in the decade: FY22 $34.4B, FY23 $12.8B, FY24 $10.1B, FY25 $13.1B, FY26 $14.5B, and FY27 $84.2M. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer for the period and a handful of vendors account for a large share of obligations. The award count and average award size suggest many smaller transactions in FY2027 to date compared with prior fiscal years that reported much larger totals. The mix of buyers and vendors in FY2027 to date highlights concentration around medical supply and specialty pharmaceutical contractors and a marked drop in overall federal spending on this NAICS code.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are buying NAICS 325412 in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $69.6M in FY2027 to date, followed by the Department of Justice with $14.6M. The Department of State recorded $0 for the period. Agency-level variation is large compared with the sector total of $84.2M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest vendors in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "CARDINAL HEALTH 414, LLC obligated $15M and MCKESSON CORPORATION obligated $14.5M in FY2027 to date. PROGENICS PHARMACEUTICALS INC obligated $12.1M and NOVARTIS PHARMACEUTICALS CORPORATION obligated $8.4M. The top ten vendors together concentrate a substantial share of the $84.2M total."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does the federal government spend on NAICS 325412?",
      "a": "The federal government obligated $84.2M on NAICS 325412 in FY2027 to date. The FY2027 to date total comes from 373 awards with an average award size of $226K, and obligations fell down 99.4% year over year. Prior fiscal years were larger: FY22 $34.4B, FY23 $12.8B, FY24 $10.1B, FY25 $13.1B, FY26 $14.5B."
